# Railway upload excludes.
#
# NOTE: a bare `node_modules` does NOT reliably match nested copies here — with
# only the top-level one excluded the payload was 618 MB / 39k files and the
# upload failed with a 500. The explicit nested patterns below keep it ~3 MB.
node_modules
**/node_modules
contracts/node_modules
server/node_modules

# Build output and caches — rebuilt on the server, never shipped.
dist
**/dist
contracts/artifacts
contracts/cache
contracts/typechain-types
*.map

# Secrets stay in Railway service variables, never in the image.
.env
.env.*

# Local state / VCS
.git
server/*.json
!server/package.json
package-lock.json

# Local runtime state, never shipped. The SQLite index lives on the Railway volume
# and is rebuilt from chain if absent, so uploading a local copy is pointless. Worse,
# it is actively being WRITTEN by any locally running backend, and a file that changes
# size while the uploader is reading it truncated the snapshot: a deploy went out at
# 629 kB with package.json and railway.json missing, and the build failed with
# "Railpack could not determine how to build the app".
# Local runtime state directory (server/store-path.js). Never part of a build.
.state/

*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
chain-index-*.json
**/chain-index-*.json
